        "original_id": "98dd9621-3bd0-5392-a81d-d82d0505f8b8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: invasion of Lae-Salamaua\n- Ships: Tama Maru No. 2, USS Lexington, USS Yorktown\n- Aircraft: Douglas SBD Dauntless, Curtiss SB2C Helldiver\n- Organizations: United States Navy, Douglas Aircraft\n- Places: Lae, New Guinea\n\nFacts:\n- Douglas Aircraft manufactured the Douglas SBD Dauntless from 1940 through 1944.\n- The Douglas SBD Dauntless was a World War II American naval scout plane and dive bomber.\n- On 10 March 1942, during the invasion of Lae-Salamaua, Douglas SBD Dauntless dive bombers from the United States Navy aircraft carriers USS Lexington and USS Yorktown damaged Tama Maru No. 2 off Lae, New Guinea.\n- The Curtiss SB2C Helldiver replaced the Douglas SBD Dauntless in United States Navy service.",
